lass=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t1-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> kilometres south of Alice Springs. Opals were first found in the area in <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t1-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> and people began to settle there after the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t1-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>. In the late 1940s, new opal fields and mass immigration from <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t1-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> created a boom, despite the extreme climate which forced about <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t1-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of the population to live underground, where they built hotels, churches, and the world's only underground <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-oxford-ielts-t1-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</p></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":6},{"id":"en-oxford-ielts-t1-l-g4-1","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 37-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Write the appropriate letters A, B, or C.</p><p>What are the l